From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:42:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Move a group call's media to a relay of the new allocation
 without a gap

Seen live: a 1:1 call became a group call on relay gru2c02; when a member
left and joined again, the server sent a group allocation listing gru1c02,
gig4c02 and poa1c01 only. The allocation refresh failed every second with
"active relay missing from group allocation", this device stayed on a relay
outside the group's set and the rejoined member never received its audio
(WhatsApp Web logged no receive relay for it). WhatsApp moves: it binds the
new relays while still on the old one and switches once the new one answers.

The media loop now runs over a switchable relay channel: sends go to the
current relay, receives come from every relay still open, and a replaced
relay keeps delivering for five seconds before it is closed; an error ends
the media only when it comes from the current relay. When an allocation no
longer lists the relay in use, a background move opens a listed relay,
sends the allocate, the consent ping and the group allocation with this
device's subscriptions, and only then switches; a failed move is retried
no sooner than ten seconds later. Each group invite and update now logs its
relay block (transaction and relay names).

Tested: the switch sends on the new relay at once, still plays packets from
the old one, closes it only after the delay, ends the media only on the
current relay's error, and Close closes every relay (race detector on);
full suite passes.
